      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given the polynomial $f(x)=3{x}^{2}+1,$ $f(3)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We substitute $x=x$ into the expression for $f(x)$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =3{x}^{2}+1 \\\\ f(3) & =3(3)^{2}+1 \\\\  & =27+1 \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(3)=28.$",
