      "dom_id": "question-74463",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Given the polynomial $g(x)={x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-4x,$ $g(1)=$",
      "worked_solution": "We substitute $x=1$ into the expression for $g(x)$ and simplify: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & ={x}^{4}+3{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-4x \\\\ g(1) & ={1}^{4}+3\\cdot {1}^{3}+{1}^{2}-4\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1+3+1-4 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(1)=1.$",
